{"height": 4, "weight": 25, "base_experience": 65, "ev_yield": [{"stat": "defense", "value": 1}], "genus": "Egg Pokémon", "capture_rate": 90, "base_happiness": 70, "hatch_counter": 20, "growth_rate": "slow", "egg_groups": ["plant"], "gender_rate": 4, "names": [{"language": "ja-hrkt", "name": "タマタマ"}, {"language": "ja-roma", "name": "Tamatama"}, {"language": "ko", "name": "아라리"}, {"language": "zh-hant", "name": "蛋蛋"}, {"language": "fr", "name": "Noeunoeuf"}, {"language": "de", "name": "Owei"}, {"language": "es", "name": "Exeggcute"}, {"language": "it", "name": "Exeggcute"}, {"language": "ja", "name": "タマタマ"}, {"language": "zh-hans", "name": "蛋蛋"}, {"language": "es-419", "name": "Exeggcute"}], "pokedex_entries": [{"versions": ["silver"], "text": "Using telepathy only they can receive, they always form a cluster of six EXEGGCUTE."}, {"versions": ["red", "blue"], "text": "Often mistaken for eggs. When disturbed, they quickly gather and attack in swarms."}, {"versions": ["yellow"], "text": "The heads attract each other and spin around. There must be 6 heads for it to maintain balance."}, {"versions": ["gold"], "text": "The shell is very durable. Even if it cracks, it can survive without spilling the contents."}, {"versions": ["crystal"], "text": "If even one is separated from the group, the energy bond between the six will make them rejoin instantly."}, {"versions": ["ruby", "sapphire"], "text": "This POKéMON consists of six eggs that form a closely knit cluster. The six eggs attract each other and spin around. When cracks increasingly appear on the eggs, EXEGGCUTE is close to evolution."}, {"versions": ["emerald"], "text": "It consists of six eggs that care for each other. The eggs attract each other and spin around. When cracks increasingly appear, it is close to evolution."}, {"versions": ["firered"], "text": "Even though it appears to be eggs of some sort, it was discovered to be a life- form more like plant seeds."}, {"versions": ["leafgreen"], "text": "It is often mistaken for eggs. When disturbed, they quickly gather and attack in swarms."}, {"versions": ["diamond", "pearl", "platinum", "black", "white", "black-2", "white-2", "x"], "text": "Its six eggs converse using telepathy. They can quickly gather if they become separated."}, {"versions": ["heartgold"], "text": "Their shells are very durable. Even if they crack, they can survive without spilling their contents."}, {"versions": ["soulsilver"], "text": "Using telepathy only they can employ, they always form a cluster of six EXEGGCUTE."}, {"versions": ["y"], "text": "Even though it appears to be eggs of some sort, it was discovered to be a life-form more like plant seeds."}, {"versions": ["omega-ruby", "alpha-sapphire"], "text": "This Pokémon consists of six eggs that form a closely knit cluster. The six eggs attract each other and spin around. When cracks increasingly appear on the eggs, Exeggcute is close to evolution."}, {"versions": ["sun"], "text": "Its six eggs use telepathy to communicate among themselves. It is believed to carry plant genes and the genes of other species."}, {"versions": ["moon"], "text": "Six of them together form a full-fledged Pokémon. It’s often hunted by Crabrawler, but uses psychokinesis to drive it off."}, {"versions": ["ultra-sun"], "text": "Six of them form a single Pokémon. Should one of the six be lost, the next morning there will once more be six."}, {"versions": ["ultra-moon"], "text": "Although they are the same size as other Exeggcute, the ones produced in Alola are quite heavy. Their shells are packed full."}, {"versions": ["lets-go-pikachu", "lets-go-eevee"], "text": "The heads attract each other and spin around. There must be six heads for it to maintain balance."}, {"versions": ["sword"], "text": "Though it may look like it’s just a bunch of eggs, it’s a proper Pokémon. Exeggcute communicates with others of its kind via telepathy, apparently."}, {"versions": ["shield"], "text": "These Pokémon get nervous when they’re not in a gro